globalThis.ragSearchTexts=globalThis.ragSearchTexts||{};globalThis.ragSearchTexts["186"]={"1547":"iaio 2026 selections for russia\n\niaio 2026 selections for russia\n\nThis competitions will be a selection that defines a team of students who will represent Russia at IAIO 2026. The problems will cover a wide range of AI topics, including different domains in machine learning and math, testing students’ practical and theoretical abilities.\n\ndata-description\nThis a test competition to help you familiarize yourself with Kaggle platform. Links to real competitions will be published in time in \"Overview\" tab of the page.\n\nThe data is quite simple: you have a set of images in `test` folder that you need to classify into 6 classes. In `train` folder there are certain examples of each class. Read \"Rules\" tab to learn more about NEOAI rules - they're going to be the same (minor changes are possible) for the rest 8 competitions you're going to participate in.\n\nYou need to write your predictions into `sample_submission.csv` file and submit it on Kaggle.\n\n**Note that this is a competition where you have a small amount of samples and you can get the ideal accuracy of 1. Try to achieve that in the least amount of submissions possible! This is the real challenge here.**\n\nWe suggest you to use Kaggle notebooks which you can create in the \"Code\" tab.\n\nabstract\nThis competitions will be a selection that defines a team of students who will represent Russia at IAIO 2026. The problems will cover a wide range of AI topics, including different domains in machine learning and math, testing students’ practical and theoretical abilities. \n\n## Dates and Format:\n**Dates:** Dec 6–9, 2025\u003cbr\u003e\n\n**Format:** Online participation with proctoring\n\u003cbr\u003e\n## Competition Structure:  \n**Dec 6** – Two ML tasks\u003cbr\u003e\n**Dec 7** - Two ML tasks\u003cbr\u003e\n**Dec 8** - Math tasks\u003cbr\u003e\n**Dec 9** - English interview\u003cbr\u003e\n\nWe like open competitions and","1548":"iaio 2026 selections for russia\n\nn with proctoring\n\u003cbr\u003e\n## Competition Structure:  \n**Dec 6** – Two ML tasks\u003cbr\u003e\n**Dec 7** - Two ML tasks\u003cbr\u003e\n**Dec 8** - Math tasks\u003cbr\u003e\n**Dec 9** - English interview\u003cbr\u003e\n\nWe like open competitions and selections, so these competitions are open to anyone - you can participate if you're not eligible (like if you're studying in university or you're not from Russia). **But note that to participate for team selection you have to register at https://form.centraluniversity.ru/IAIO_wait_list/ before December 5th 18:00 MSK**.\n\nTasks will be gradually released according to the following schedule:  \n\n| Task   | Available From      | Available Until     | Link                       |\n|--------|---------------------|---------------------|----------------------------|\n| ML Task 1 | Dec 6, 09:00 MSK    | Dec 6, 11:00 MSK    | https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/iaio-2026-sfr-timeseries-classification |\n| ML Task 2 | Dec 6, 11:30 MSK    | Dec 6, 15:30 MSK    | https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/iaio-2026-sf-r-recommend-music |\n| ML Task 3 | Dec 7, 09:00 MSK    | Dec 7, 12:00 MSK    | https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/iaio-2026-sf-r-comments-classification  |\n| ML Task 4 | Dec 7, 13:00 MSK    | Dec 7, 17:00 MSK    | https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/iaio-2026-sf-r-image-classification |\n| Math tasks part 1 | Dec 8, 09:00 MSK    | Dec 8, 11:00 MSK    |  |\n| Math tasks part 2 | Dec 8, 12:00 MSK    | Dec 8, 14:00 MSK    |  |\n\n## Rules\nCarefully read \"Rules\" section before joining the competitions.","1918":"Отбор России на IAIO 2026\nhttps://www.kaggle.com/competitions/iaio-2026-selections-for-russia\n\nКраткое описание:\nАрхив российского отбора на зимнюю международную олимпиаду IAIO 2026 на Kaggle. Отбор уже прошёл; контест сохранён для тренировки.\n\nПодтверждения владельца:\nKaggle-контест iaio-2026-selections-for-russia в №186 сохранён как архив прошедшего российского отбора IAIO 2026 для тренировки, а не как текущий отбор."};
